window.DeskData.define("desk/drafts/precedent-64770257e313.json",{"text":"JOINT VENTURE AND SHAREHOLDERS AGREEMENT\n\n\n\n\tAmong\n\n\n\n[Name of Hollard Insurance Entity] (“IVM”),\n\n\n\n[VISHAL RETAIL LIMITED] (“VISHAL”),\n\nAND\n\n[MR. RAM CHANDRA AGARWAL] (“RCA”).\n\n\n\n   \n\n\n\n\n\n\tDated as of  April [●], 2008\n\n\n\n\n                               \n   JOINT VENTURE AND SHAREHOLDERS AGREEMENT\n\nTHIS JOINT VENTURE AND SHAREHOLDERS AGREEMENT (this “Agreement”) is entered into as of April [●], 2008, by and among:\n\n[Name of Hollard Insurance Entity], a trust established under the laws of the Netherlands, having its principal office at ________________________, Netherlands (hereinafter referred to as “IVM”, which expression shall where the context so admits include its successors, administrators, trustees and assigns), of the FIRST PART;\n\nAND\n\nVISHAL RETAIL LIMITED, a company incorporated under the Companies Act, 1956, having its registered office at ________________________, India, through its authorized signatory, Mr. ______________  (hereinafter referred to as “VRL” which expression shall where the context so admits include its successors and permitted assigns), of the SECOND PART;\n\nAND\n\nMR. RAM CHANDRA AGARWAL, son of Late Shri Kishan Gopal Agarwal, resident of B1-801, Lagoon Apartments, Ambience Islands, Gurgaon, Haryana, India (hereinafter referred to as “RCA” which expression shall where the context so admits include his heirs, legal representatives and permitted assigns), of the THIRD PART.\n\nVRL and RCA are hereinafter sometimes collectively referred to as “Vishal”. Hollard and Vishal are herein sometimes collectively referred to as the “Parties” and singly as a “Party”.\n\nRECITALS\n\nWHEREAS, Hollard and its Affiliates are engaged in the business of designing and creating insurance based solutions for select organizations and retailers of consumer goods and services. \n\nWHEREAS, VRL is part of the Vishal Group, one of India’s fastest growing retail businesses of consumer goods and services. As part of its retail endeavours, VRL has more than ten (10) warehouses catering to over a hundred (100) retail outlets in twenty (20) states and sixty seven (67) cities in India. RCA is one of the founding members of VRL, owning approximately [●%] of the issued and paid up share capital of VRL.\n\nWHEREAS, the Parties wish to establish a joint venture company (the “JV Company”) which will undertake to (i) procure, maintain, process and sub-license data bases which are relevant to insurance in the retail industries markets and also to the business of the JV Company, (ii) provide business process and data processing services in insurance in the retail markets, (iii) provide advisory and consultancy services to insurance intermediaries and insurers including without limitation in the areas of customer relationship management, international markets, record maintenance, product selection, direct marketing and promotions, product design, etc., and (iv) provide advisory and consultancy services to retailers including without limitation in the areas of customer relationship management, customer promotional schemes, channel management, etc. \n\nWHEREAS, the Parties believe it is desirable and in their mutual interests to set forth their agreements with respect to the formation and management of the JV Company, their respective duties and obligations, the transferability of their respective interests therein, and other matters. \n\nNOW THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual promises and agreements contained herein, the Parties intending to be bound legally, agree as follows.\n\nARTICLE I\nDEFINITIONS \n\n1.01\tDefined Terms: As used herein, the following terms shall have the following respective meanings:\n\n    (a) “Affiliate” as to any Party, means (a) any other Person which, directly or indirectly, is in control of, is controlled by, or is under common control with such Person; or (b) any other Person owning beneficially or controlling, directly or indirectly, fifty percent (50%) or more of the equity interest in such Person; or (c) any Person who is a director, officer or partner of such Person; or (d) any spouse or Relative of such Person. For purposes of this definition, control of a Person shall mean the possession of the power, direct or indirect, to direct or cause the direction of the management and policies of a Person, whether through the ownership of partnership interests or voting securities, by contract or otherwise. The term \"Relative\" shall have the meaning ascribed to it in Section 6 of the Companies Act.\n\n    (b) “Board of Directors” or “Board” means the board of directors of the JV Company.\n\n    (c) “Business Day” means any day excluding Sunday and any day which shall be a gazetted holiday.\n\n    (d) “Buyback Notice” shall have the meaning ascribed to it in Section 14.02(b)(i) below.\n\n    (e) “Call Notice” shall have the meaning ascribed to it in Section 6.03(b) below.\n\n    (f) “Call Notice I” shall have the meaning ascribed to it in Section 14.02(b)(iii) below.\n\n    (g) “Call Option” shall have the meaning ascribed to it in Section 6.03 below.\n\n    (h) “Companies Act” means the Companies Act, 1956, including all amendments, restatements, modifications or supplements thereto.\n\n    (i) “Closing” means the subscription by IVM for the IVM Shares as contemplated in terms of Section 5.01 below.\n\n    (j) “Conditions Precedent” means the conditions precedent stated in Article IV below.\n\n    (k) “Closing Date” means the [●] day of [●], 2008, or such other date as may be agreed in writing by the Parties.\n\n    (l) “Deadlock Situation” means, with respect to any matter to be decided either at a meeting of the Board or at any meeting of any committee thereof, or by the Shareholders at a General Meeting of the JV Company, that the votes cast in favour and the votes cast against such matter are equal. Deadlock Situations shall be resolved in the manner provided for in this Agreement.\n\n    (m) “Deed of Adherence” means an agreement between an Affiliate or a third party, as the case may be, and the Parties, in terms of this Agreement, in the form annexed to this Agreement as Exhibit A.\n\n    (n) “Defaulting Shareholding” shall have the meanings ascribed to it in Section 14.02(a) and Section 14.02(b) below.\n\n    (o) “Director” means a director of the Board of Directors and includes an Alternate Director.\n\n    (p) “Effective Date” means the date of execution of this Agreement.\n\n    (q) “FEMA Regulations” shall have the meaning ascribed to it in Section 6.02(a) below.\n\n    (r) “General Meeting” shall have the meaning ascribed to it in Section 8.01 below.\n\n    (s) “Independent Valuer” shall have the meaning ascribed to it in Section 11.02(a) below.\n\n    (t) “India GAAP” means generally accepted accounting principles in India as in effect from time to time.\n\n    (u) “Lock-In-Period” shall have the meaning ascribed to it in Section 11.01 below.\n\n    (v) “New Shares” mean any Shares, whether now authorized or not, and rights, options or warrants to purchase such Shares, and securities of any type whatsoever that are, or may become, convertible or exchangeable into such Shares.\n\n    (w) “Organizational Documents” mean the Articles of Association and Memorandum of Association of the JV Company.\n\n    (x) “Parties” mean IVM and Vishal and “Party” means individually IVM and Vishal. \n\n    (y) “Person” means any individual, firm, corporation, company, trust, society, partnership, association, joint venture, unincorporated organization or other business entity.\n\n    (z) “Put Notice” shall have the meaning ascribed to it in Section 14.02(b)(ii) below.\n\n    (aa) “ROC” means the Registrar of Companies, National Capital Territory of Delhi & Haryana. \n\n    (bb) “Selling Shareholder” has the meaning ascribed to in Section 11.02(a) below.\n\n    (cc) “Selling Shareholder Notice” has the meaning ascribed to it in Section 11.02(a) below.\n\n    (dd) “Shares” mean the shares comprised in the share capital of the JV Company and includes the VRL Shares, RCA Shares and the IVM Shares, and having the rights attached to them as described in this Agreement and in the Organizational Documents.\n\n    (ee) “Shareholder Representative” shall have the meaning ascribed to it in Section 8.02 below.\n\n    (ff) “Shareholding Interest” shall mean, with respect to each Shareholder, the interest of such Shareholder in the share capital of the JV Company derived by dividing the total number of shares registered in the name of such Shareholder by the total issued and paid up shares, on a fully diluted basis. \n\n    (gg) “Shareholders” mean the Parties and any other purchaser, transferee or owner, beneficial or otherwise, of Shares of the JV Company, and “Shareholder” shall be construed accordingly.\n\n    (hh) “Transfer” means a direct or indirect transfer, sale, assignment, mortgage, hypothecation, pledge, creation of a security interest in or lien upon, encumbrance, donation, placement in trust, or other voluntary or involuntary disposal of Shares or any interest therein.\n\n    (ii) “Transferee” means a Person to whom a Transfer is made in accordance with the terms of this Agreement.\n\n    (jj) “Transferring Shareholder” means any Shareholder making a Transfer or proposing a Transfer.\n\n    (kk) “Vishal Channels” mean the established market mechanism of VRL including its retail and distribution channels (now existing or to be developed in the future) for distributing and selling products to VRL’s end consumers. \n\n    (ll) “Warrantors” and “Warrantor” shall have the meanings ascribed to them in Section 7.01 below.\n\n1.02\tRules of Construction. In the interpretation of this Agreement, unless the context otherwise requires:  \n\n\t(a)\tthe singular includes the plural and vice versa, and in particular (but without limiting the generality of the foregoing) any word or expression defined in the singular has the corresponding meaning used in the plural and vice versa;\n\n\t(b)\ta reference to any gender includes the other gender;\n\n\t(c)\ta reference to any agreement is a reference to that agreement and all exhibits, schedules, appendices and the like incorporated therein, as the same is amended, modified, supplemented, waived, varied, added to, substituted, replaced, renewed or extended from time to time;\n\n\t(d)\ta reference to statutes shall be construed as including all statutory provisions consolidating, amending, modifying, supplementing or replacing the statute referred to;\n\n\t(e)\tthe terms “include”, “including” and “among other things” shall be deemed to be followed by the words “without limitation” or “but not limited to” whether or not so followed;\n\n\t(f)\tany reference to a Person or entity shall include such Person's and such entity's successors and permitted assigns, and shall include all natural persons, corporations, companies, and partnerships and other legal entities; and\n\n\t(g)\ta reference to “writing” includes printing, typing, lithography and other means of reproducing words in a visible form.\n\nARTICLE II\nFORMATION OF JV COMPANY\n\n2.01\tFormation of the JV Company.  Prior to the Closing, Vishal, on behalf of the Parties, will cause a private limited liability company called “_____________”, or such other name as the Parties may mutually agree, to be incorporated in accordance with the Companies Act, and otherwise in accordance with the laws of India. The registered office of the JV Company shall be located at ____________________________________________.  As is more fully set forth in the Memorandum and Articles of Association, the JV Company shall have one class of share capital, i.e., equity shares, and its authorized capital shall consist of 1,00,000 (One Lakh) equity shares, par value Rs. 10/- each. Notwithstanding the issuance of the certificate of incorporation, the JV Company shall not commence business nor exercise any borrowing powers until the Closing Date.\n\n2.02\tBusiness.  As is more fully set forth in the Memorandum of Association of the JV Company, the business and main objects of the JV Company will be to (i) procure, maintain, process and sub-license data bases which are relevant to insurance in the retail industries markets and also to the business of the JV Company, (ii) provide business process and data processing services in insurance in the retail markets, (iii) provide advisory and consultancy services to insurance intermediaries and insurers including without limitation in the areas of customer relationship management, international markets, record maintenance, product selection, direct marketing and promotions, product design, etc., and (iv) provide advisory and consultancy services to retailers including without limitation in the areas of customer relationship management, customer promotional schemes, channel management, etc.\n\n2.03\tBusiness Plan. The JV Company shall conduct its business in accordance with a business plan as created in accordance with Section 6.04(a)(i) and as may be amended from time to time in accordance with Section 12.02 hereof (the “Business Plan”). \n\n2.04\tPre-Closing Equity Ownership.  Prior to the Closing, VRL and RCA each will make application for equity shares as set forth below, and upon the making of such applications and the making of the capital contributions by the relevant Party as set forth below, the JV Company shall allot and issue to VRL and RCA equity shares of the JV Company as follows:\n\nName of Shareholder\tNo. of Equity Shares\n \tShareholding Interest\nVRL \t[●] equity shares\t[●] %\nRCA\t[●] equity shares\t[●] %\nTOTAL\t50,000 Equity Shares\t100%\n\nThe Shares issued to VRL are hereinafter referred to as the “VRL Shares” while the Shares issued to RCA are hereinafter referred to as the “RCA Shares”. Vishal shall ensure that no other Shares are issued or allotted other than as provided for in this Agreement.\n\nARTICLE III\nSHARE SUBSCRIPTION\n\n3.01\tShare Subscription. On the Closing Date and subject to fulfillment, to the satisfaction of IVM or waiver thereof in writing by IVM, of the Conditions Precedent stated in Article IV below, IVM shall subscribe for, and Vishal shall procure and cause the JV Company to issue and allot to IVM [50,000] equity shares of the face value of Rs. 10/ each, at Rs. [800] per share, i.e., a premium of Rs. 790/- per equity share (hereafter the “IVM Shares”). The amount paid by IVM for the IVM Shares, i.e., Rs. [4,00,00,000], is hereinafter referred to as the “IVM Subscription Price”.\n\n30.2\tShareholding Structure. After the issue of the IVM Shares to IVM, the paid up share capital of the JV Company on a fully diluted basis shall be as follows:\n\nName of Shareholder\tNo. of Equity Shares\n \tShareholding Interest\nVRL \t[●] equity shares\t[●] %\nRCA \t[●] equity shares\t[●] %\nIVM\t50,000 equity shares\t50%\nTOTAL\t1,00,000 Equity Shares\t100%\n\nARTICLE IV\nCONDITIONS PRECEDENT TO CLOSING\n\n4.01\tConditions Precedent. IVM’s obligation to consummate the transactions contemplated in this Agreement and subscribe for, and purchase the IVM Shares, is subject to the determination by IVM in its sole discretion that the following conditions have been satisfied, on or prior to the Closing:\n\n    (a) The representations and warranties of VIshal and RCA set forth in Article VII below shall be true and correct as of the Closing Date with the same force and effect as if they had been made as of the Closing Date.\n\n    (b) The allotment, issuance and purchase of the IVM Shares shall be legally permitted by all agreements, laws and regulations to which the Parties are subject.\n\n    (c) All necessary corporate authorizations including, but not limited to, approval of the Board of Directors of the JV Company, for the JV Company to perform its obligations and consummate the transactions contemplated herein, including the issue of the IVM Shares, shall have been obtained. \n\n    (d) All necessary corporate authorizations including, but not limited to, approval of the Board of Directors of VRL for VRL to perform its obligations and consummate the transactions contemplated herein shall have been obtained. \n\n    (e) All necessary corporate authorizations including, but not limited to, approval of the Board of Directors of IVM for IVM to perform its obligations and consummate the transactions contemplated herein shall have been obtained.\n\n    (f) There shall not have been any change in such of the JV Company’s affairs, assets, liabilities, financial condition or business, as would materially and adversely affect the JV Company’s conduct of its business.\n\n    (g) No action or proceeding or litigation including without limitation, civil or criminal actions shall be pending or threatened in India or elsewhere by any Person, entity or governmental authority against the JV Company and/or VRL or RCA to enjoin or prohibit the performance of any of the transactions contemplated hereunder, including without limitation conduct of the JV Company’s business.\n\n    (h) The JV Company shall have delivered to IVM such documents including but not limited to the following:\n\n(i) \tCertified copies of the Memorandum of Association and Articles of Association of the JV Company along with the Certificate of Incorporation of the JV Company; \n\n(ii) \tCopy of agreement executed by the JV Company upon its incorporation agreeing to be bound to this terms and conditions of this Agreement in form and substance attached hereto as Exhibit B as if it were originally a party hereto; \n\n(iii)\tCertified copy of the resolution of the Board of Directors of the JV Company authorizing the due execution of the agreement referred to in sub-section (h) (ii) above and consummation of the transactions contemplated in this Agreement; \n\n(iv) \tCertified copies of the notices convening a meeting of the Shareholders of the JV Company and of the Board of Directors of the JV Company on the Closing Date, to take the actions specified in Section 5.02 below; and\n\n(v) \ta no objection certificate, in the form attached hereto as Exhibit C, from each of VRL and RCA and the JV Company.\n\nIn case any of the foregoing conditions shall not be fulfilled as of the Closing Date, IVM may rescind this Agreement by written notice to VIshal and RCA and in such event IVM shall be released from all obligations hereunder without any financial liability on IVM whatsoever; Provided that any of the conditions of this Section 4.01 may be waived in whole or in part by IVM upon written notice to VRL and RCA without prejudice to IVM’s rights of rescission in the event of the non-fulfillment of any other condition or conditions. Any waiver hereunder shall be binding only if it is in writing.  \n\nARTICLE V\nCLOSING; ACTIONS AT CLOSING\n\n5.01\tClosing:  On the Closing Date, and subject to satisfactory fulfillment of all the Conditions Precedent stated in Article IV above or waiver thereof in writing by IVM, IVM shall subscribe to, and Vishal shall procure and cause the JV Company to issue and allot to IVM the IVM Shares, and \n\n    (a) IVM shall remit/wire transfer the amount of the IVM Subscription Price for the IVM Shares to the JV Company or cause the IVM Subscription Price to be transferred into the JV Company’s bank account; and\n\n    (b) VIshal and RCA shall procure the JV Company to allot and issue to IVM, the IVM Shares, for cash consideration, on a fully diluted basis, fully paid up and free and clear of any security interest, lien, pledge, claim, encumbrance, restriction or right of third parties of any kind whatsoever, and shall deliver to IVM duly issued original share certificates evidencing the IVM Shares. \n\n5.02\tActions at Closing. On the Closing Date, Vishal shall take/procure the occurrence of following actions: \n\n(a) Convene a meeting of the Board of Directors of the JV Company at which the following shall be resolved by passing appropriate resolutions:\n\n(i) \tTo allot and issue the IVM Shares to IVM, amounting to 50% of the issued and paid up share capital of the JV Company (determined on a fully diluted basis) at a purchase price of Rs. [800] per share. \n\n(ii)\tTo appoint Mr. Ian Ross and Mr. Ajay Budhiraja, nominees of IVM, as Directors on the Board of Directors of the JV Company and to make all necessary filings in Form No. 32 with the ROC. \n\n(iii)\tTo record the name of IVM in its Register of Members as the legal and beneficial owner of the IVM Shares and to make all necessary filings with the ROC including Returns of Allotment. \n \n5.02 \tActions after Closing. Not more than thirty (30) Business Days after the Closing Date the Parties shall agree on revisions to the Articles of Association of the JV Company to reflect relevant provisions of this Agreement including all rights attached to the IVM Shares. The Parties shall cause their respective nominees on the Board to approve such revised Articles of Association and recommend the revised Articles of Association to the Shareholders for their adoption at an extra ordinary general meeting. The Parties shall also cause their respective nominees on the Board of Directors to convene an extra ordinary general meeting of the Shareholders of the JV Company at shorter notice (in any event not later than thirty (30) Business Days after the Closing Date), to which the Shareholders shall have no objection, at which it will be resolved to adopt the revised Articles of Association as presented by the Board of Directors. \n\n5.03\tDeliveries after Closing. Within thirty five (35) Business Days of the Closing Date, Vishal shall deliver to IVM certified true copies of the following documents: \n\n    (a) statutory filings with the ROC with regard to the (i) adoption of the revised set of Articles of Association, and (ii) appointment of Mr. Ian Ross and Mr. Ajay Budhiraja, nominees of IVM, to the Board of Directors of the JV Company in terms of Section 5.02(a)(ii) above, including without limitation Form Nos. 23 and 32, and the treasury receipts issued by the ROC evidencing such filings with the ROC; \n\n    (b) Extracts of the Register of Members of the JV Company on the Closing Date; and\n\n    (c) Resolutions of the Board of Directors and Shareholders of the JV Company referred to in Section 5.02 (a) above. \n\n5.04\tCalculation Of Fully-Diluted Equity. Except as expressly stated herein, all references herein to calculations of the JV Company's Shares thereof as then outstanding “on a fully diluted basis” or as “fully diluted” or similar terms shall mean such Shares at any date as diluted by the issuance of all Shares then issuable upon the exercise or conversion of all then outstanding and exercisable warrants, options or convertible securities pursuant to which the JV Company is then obligated to issue such equity or type or class thereof (and if such exercise or conversion results in the issuance of convertible securities, as further diluted by the conversion of such convertible securities). For the purposes of determining the number of Shares held by any Shareholder on a fully-diluted basis hereunder at any time, such Shareholder shall be deemed to hold that number of Shares as is equal to (i) the number of issued Shares then held by such Shareholder plus (ii) the number of Shares ultimately issuable upon conversion or exercise of any other outstanding securities then held by such Shareholder.\n\n5.05\tInvestment by IVM. It is hereby agreed that for purposes of investment by IVM in the share capital of the JV Company and subscription to, and purchase of the IVM Shares and participation in any subsequent funding of the JV Company, IVM may elect and nominate any of its Affiliates to exercise the right to invest in the share capital of the JV Company and subscribe to, and/or acquire Shares of the JV Company and/or to own/hold any Shares subscribed to by IVM including the IVM Shares, to which the Parties shall have no objection and IVM’s Shareholding Interest shall be accordingly construed to include its direct and indirect shareholding held by its Affiliates; provided that any such Affiliate shall execute and deliver a Deed of Adherence to the Parties in the form and substance as annexed to this Agreement in Exhibit A. \n\nARTICLE VI\nCOVENANTS; OTHER AGREEMENTS\n\n6.01\tAnti-Dilution Rights.  Except as may be expressly provided in this Agreement and/or mutually agreed among the Parties in writing, it is agreed that pursuant to the issue of, and purchase of the IVM Shares, IVM shall be entitled to maintain its Shareholding Interest in the JV Company and the JV Company shall not undertake any issue of New Shares unless the same is being offered to all holders of Shares in the manner stated in Section 81(1) of the Companies Act. \n\n6.02\tLoans by IVM & its Affiliates. In addition to its investment in the share capital of the JV Company, IVM shall on a best endeavour basis, and upon request by the JV Company from time to time, arrange to either itself or through its Affiliates provide the JV Company such amounts as may be required by the JV Company upto an amount of US$ 1,000,000 million (United States Dollars One Million only) by way of subordinated limited recourse loans. Provided that: \n\n(a)\tany loan provided by IVM shall be subject to compliance with regulations as may be prescribed by the Foreign Exchange Management Act, 1999 and Regulations issued thereunder, with respect to external commercial borrowings (“FEMA Regulations”); \n\n(b)\tthe JV Company shall give IVM at least thirty (30) Business Days written notice stating the amount required and the proposed disbursement date which shall not be less than forty five (45) Business Days from the date of issue of the written notice;\n\n(c)\tthe JV Company will enter into a loan agreement with IVM on terms and conditions as to repayment as may be mutually agreed upon, subject to compliance with applicable law. The principal amount of any loan shall be repaid on a monthly basis over twelve (12) months commencing after six (6) months of the JV Company achieving operating profits. The principal amount of the loan may also be repaid in one lump sum at any time after the JV Company achieves operating profits, subject to the business needs of the JV Company as determined by the Board;\n\n(d)\tany loan amount in excess of an amount of US$ 1,000,000 million (United States Dollars One Million only) or its Rupee equivalent shall be subject to a unanimous resolution of the Board;\n\n(e)\tsubject to compliance with FEMA Regulations, the loan will operate as a revolving loan so that it can be repaid and redrawn; and\n\n(f)\tsubject to the JV Company continuing to carry on its business, any loan so provided by IVM shall be repaid from out of the profits of the JV Company, prior to declaration and distribution of dividends to the Shareholders. In case the JV Company has ceased carrying on business, the loan amount shall be repaid subject to priority amongst creditors and statutory dues.\n\n\t6.03\tGrant of Option. Subject to Vishal’s right to exit their shareholding in the JV Company prior to the expiry of the Lock-In-Period as stated in Section 11.01, VRL and RCA hereby grant IVM an irrevocable option (however, not an obligation), exercisable by IVM in its sole discretion, to purchase all but not less than all of the VRL Shares and the RCA Shares at the fair market value for such Shares (hereafter the “Call Option”) as determined by the Independent Valuer appointed in terms of Section 11.02(a) below. The Call Option shall be subject to the following:\n\n    (a) The Call Option shall be exercisable by IVM if at any time prior to the expiry of the Lock-In-Period VRL and/or RCA proposes to exit from the JV Company (as evidenced by proposed sale of the VRL Shares or the RCA Shares, as the case may be, or otherwise). \n\n    (b) IVM shall be entitled to exercise the Call Option by issuing a written notice (“Call Notice”), specifying that it will purchase the VRL Shares and the RCA Shares at the price being the fair market value of the Shares as determined by the Independent Valuer. In the event IVM exercises the Call Option as aforesaid, the Parties shall, within fifteen (15) Business Days from the issue of the Call Notice obtain a valuation of the VRL Shares and RCA Shares from the Independent Valuer. The Independent Valuer shall be instructed not to include the amount of any premium paid by IVM for the IVM Shares for purposes of determining the fair market value of the Shares. VRL and RCA shall thereafter be obliged to sell to IVM the VRL Shares and the RCA Shares respectively at the fair market value for such Shares so determined by the Independent Valuer. The purchase by IVM of the VRL Shares and the RCA Shares shall be completed on a spot delivery basis on a date which shall be no later than sixty (60) Business Days from the date of issue of the Call Notice by IVM upon VRL and RCA. It is clarified that IVM shall be entitled to purchase the VRL Shares and the RCA Shares either directly or designate nominee(s) for this purpose.\n\n    (c) At the closing of such Share purchase, VRL and RCA shall simultaneously with the payment for the Shares (which are subject matter of the Call Notice), by IVM, deliver or cause to be delivered to IVM and/or its nominee(s), duly executed share transfer deeds, share certificates and do such things and execute such other documents as shall be necessary, or as IVM and/or its nominee(s) may reasonably request, to give effect to the sale of such Shares. \n\n    (d) Upon the sale of the VRL Shares and the RCA Shares as aforesaid, IVM shall procure that within ninety (90) Business Days of such sale, the JV Company ceases to use any name, or brand or logo of Vishal. Provided, however, that VRL and RCA shall enter into and execute appropriate agreements as may be required by the JV Company to continue to meet its contractual obligations to its existing customers/clients.\n\n6.04\tResponsibilities of the Parties. It is hereby agreed among the Parties that the following are the responsibilities of the Parties without any additional costs to the JV Company:\n\n\t(a)\tIVM’s Responsibilities.\n\n\t(i) \tIVM shall be responsible for preparing a Business Plan for the JV Company from time to time during the term of this Agreement in consultation with Vishal. The Business Plan shall have a tenure of thirty six (36) calendar months. This Business Plan will define the operational details of the JV Company and will include, but not be limited to, items such as budgets, forecasts, capital expenditures, salaries and wages, other operational costs, required resources, target clients/customers, market information (services, pricing, discounts, etc). The Plan will serve the purpose of giving management direction as to the day-to-day operation of the JV Company. IVM shall endeavour to submit a Business Plan for the Board’s approval within sixty (60) Business Days of the Closing Date. IVM shall endeavour to ensure that the factual information given in a Business Plan will be correct and that any forecast reflects reasonable business judgement. Other than the representations and warranties provided herein, IVM gives no warranties, guarantees or assurances with respect to any Business Plan;\n\n\t(ii) \tIVM shall identify potential customers/clients for the JV Company’s services,  and will consider appropriate services to be provided to them by the JV Company;\n\n(iii)\tIVM shall continually explore new areas of consulting and advisory services which may be provided by the JV Company, subject to compliance with then existing applicable regulations. New areas of consulting and advisory services shall be informally discussed with Vishal and a business plan appropriately prepared and developed. Discussions with Vishal on new areas of services shall be on the following parameters, viz. description of such services, feasibility of JV Company providing such services, suitability of such services for identified potential customers/clients, costs of preparing a business plan for such services, and the proposed date of commencement/delivery of such services by the JV Company; \n\n(iv)\tIVM shall be responsible for management analysis and allocation of responsibilities amongst the Parties with respect to the business of the JV Company; \n\n(v)\tSubject to the provisions of Section 10.02 below, IVM shall be responsible for the day to day management, operations and business of the JV Company, including without limitation staffing of the officers and other personnel of JV Company, remuneration to be paid to JV Company’s employees, business operations, training of JV Company’s employees, etc.;\n\n(vi) \tIVM shall ensure that any business carried on, entered into or proposed to be entered into by the JV Company, will inure solely for the benefit of the JV Company and the income of the JV Company shall not be diverted for the benefit of any other Person. In this regard, IVM hereby indemnifies and hold harmless Vishal from any loss of earnings to Vishal arising out of a diversion of the business/profit of the JV Company directly attributable to IVM. The amount of the indemnity shall not exceed twice the amount of loss of earnings to Vishal. \n\n\t(b)\tVishal’s Responsibilities.\n\n\t(i) \tVishal undertakes to make available to the JV Company, and provide the JV Company access to the Vishal Channels for use by the JV Company for marketing and complimenting the services of the JV Company;\n\n(ii)\tVishal undertakes to make available to the JV Company and JV Company’s customers, and provide the JV Company and JV Company’s customers access to allied physical and information technology infrastructure of Vishal as per the requirements of the JV Company and approved by the Board. \n\n(iii) \tVishal undertakes to grant a license of its retail and distribution databases to JV Company for the use of the JV Company for marketing and complimenting the services of the JV Company with identified customers/clients, with a right to the JV Company to sub-license the same to its customers/clients with notice to Vishal. The Parties shall procure and ensure that Vishal’s data base shall not be misused by the JV Company. Vishal undertakes and warrants that its grant of license to the JV Company as aforesaid shall not violate any confidential information obligations or other contractual obligations of Vishal or any other applicable laws;\n\n(iv) \tVishal undertakes to provide all reasonable marketing support to the JV Company. In this regard, Vishal shall promote the JV Company and/or JV Company’s customers wherever possible in its advertising promotions while the Parties shall procure the JV Company to promote the VRL brand through the JV Company’s marketing efforts;  \n\n(v) \tSubject to IVM’s consent, which shall not be unreasonably withheld, Vishal may also propose new areas of consulting and advisory services which may be provided by the JV Company. Any such agreed proposals shall then be developed by IVM. No Party shall withhold potential areas of services for the JV Company. Vishal shall endeavour to ensure that the factual information provided to IVM for use in a Business Plan will be correct and that any forecast provided to IVM reflects reasonable business judgement.\n\n6.05\tMutual Co-operation and Assistance to the JV Company. Each Party agrees that it will use all reasonable endeavors to promote the business and profitability of  the JV Company. Each of the Parties shall do and execute or procure to be done and executed all such acts, deeds, documents and things as may be within its power including (without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing) in relation to the passing of resolutions (whether by the Board or in General Meeting of the JV Company) to give full effect to this Agreement and to procure that all provisions of this Agreement are observed and performed. Each Party agrees with the other that this Agreement is entered into between them and will be performed by each of them in a spirit of mutual co-operation, trust and confidence and that it will use all means reasonably available to it (including its/his voting power whether direct or indirect, in relation to the JV Company) to give effect to the objectives of this Agreement and to ensure compliance by the JV Company with its obligations. \n\n\t6.06\tNon-Compete. Subject to the provisions of Section 14.04(e) below, during the subsistence of this Agreement and for as long as VRL and/or RCA owns any Shares of the JV Company and one (1) year thereafter, whichever is later, VRL and  RCA, jointly and severally, represent and warrant as follows:\n\n(a)\tneither they nor their Affiliates/Relatives will have any direct or indirect ownership in or will serve as a proprietor, partner, officer, director, employee, sales representative, consultant of, or for any entity/person or party that competes with the business of the JV Company; or \n\n(b)\tneither they nor their Affiliates/Relatives will, directly or indirectly, enter into any agreement, arrangement, sharing or relationship by whatever name called with any Person for providing services similar to those provided by the JV Company; or\n\n(c)\tneither they nor their Affiliates/Relatives will solicit or entice or endeavour to solicit or entice away from the JV Company any customer or trade connection of the JV Company whether or not such customer or trade connection would commit a breach of contract by reason of terminating such relationship; or\n\n(d)\tneither they nor their Affiliates/Relatives will cause or permit any Person directly or indirectly under their control to do any of the things set out in Sections 6.05(a), 6.05(b) and 6.05(c) above.\n\n\tProvided that the provisions of this Section 6.06 shall not apply if this Agreement is terminated by mutual written agreement of the Shareholders in terms of Section 14.01 below.\n\nARTICLE VII\nREPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES\n\n7.01\tRepresentations and Warranties of VRL and RCA. VRL and RCA (for the purposes of this Article, VRL and RCA are collectively referred to as the “Warrantors” and singly as a “Warrantor”) hereby jointly and severally represent and warrant to IVM as of the Effective Date and the Closing Date as follows:\n\n(a)\tThe JV Company will be duly incorporated under the laws of India and upon incorporation, will have all requisite power and authority, corporate or otherwise, to enter into and to perform its obligations hereunder and to carry out the terms hereof and the transactions contemplated hereby, to own and operate its properties and assets and to carry on its business as currently conducted and as presently proposed to be conducted.  \n\n\t(b)\tEach Warrantor is competent to enter into this Agreement and the execution, delivery and performance by the Warrantors of this Agreement  and the consummation of the transactions contemplated hereby, will not result in any violation of the terms of any material contract or agreement to which the Warrantors are/were jointly and/or severally bound, or of any license, permit, franchise, judgment, writ, injunction or regulation, decree, order, charter, law, ordinance, rule or regulation applicable, jointly and/or severally to the Warrantors or any of their respective properties or to any obligations incurred by them or by which they or any of their properties or obligations are bound or affected, or of any determination or award of any arbitrator applicable to them, and will not conflict with, or cause a breach of, or default under, any such term or result in the creation of any lien upon any of their properties or assets.\n\n\t(c)\tThe execution, delivery and performance of this Agreement by VRL has been duly authorized by all necessary corporate action required under the Companies Act, on the part of the JV Company and do not require any approval or consent of any Person. The execution, delivery and performance by VRL of this Agreement and the consummation of the transactions contemplated hereby, will not result in any violation of any term of its Memorandum of Association or Articles of Association, as the case may be, or any material contract or agreement applicable to it, or of any license, permit, franchise, judgment, writ, injunction or regulation, decree, order, charter, law, ordinance, rule or regulation applicable to it or any of its properties or to any obligations incurred by it or by which it or any of its properties or obligations are bound or affected, or of any determination or award of any arbitrator applicable to it, and will not conflict with, or cause a breach of, or default under, any such term or result in the creation of any lien upon any of its properties or assets. \n\n\t(d)\tThis Agreement has been duly executed and delivered by the Warrantors and constitutes the legal, valid and binding obligation of the Warrantors, enforceable against them respectively in accordance with its terms, as such enforceability may be limited by applicable bankruptcy, insolvency, reorganization, moratorium and similar laws affecting creditors’ rights generally.\n\n\t(e)\tThere is no legislation, action, suit, proceeding or investigation pending or, to the best of the Warrantors’ knowledge, threatened, before or by any court, administrative agency, environmental council, arbitrator or governmental authority, body or agency against the Warrantors which could reasonably be expected to materially and adversely affect the performance by such Warrantor of such Warrantor’s obligations hereunder or which questions the validity, binding effect or enforceability hereof or, any action taken or to be taken by such Warrantor pursuant hereto or any of the transactions contemplated hereby.\n\n\t(f)\tThe IVM Shares, when issued in terms of this Agreement, will be validly issued, fully paid and not subject to, or issued in violation of, any pre-emptive rights. \n\n(g)\tThe Warrantors acknowledge that IVM is a foreign investor under the relevant regulatory regime. Warrantors agree and undertake not to procure or cause the JV Company to carry on, any business for which the investment by IVM is prohibited under prevailing regulatory regime/policy and/or which adversely or materially affects IVM’s investment in the JV Company as a foreign investment. \n\n(h)\tThe representations, warranties and statements made by the Warrantors in or pursuant to this Agreement are true, complete and correct in all material respects and do not contain any untrue statement of a material fact or omit to state any material fact necessary to make any such representation, warranty or statement, under the circumstances in which it is made, not misleading.  \n\n7.02\tRepresentations and Warranties of IVM. IVM hereby represents and warrants, to the Warrantor as of the Effective Date and the Closing Date as follows:\n\n    (a) IVM is duly organized incorporated and validly existing in good standing under the laws of Netherlands and has all requisite power and authority, corporate or otherwise, to enter into and to perform its obligations hereunder and to carry out the terms hereof and the transactions contemplated hereby. \n\n    (b) This Agreement has been duly executed and delivered on behalf of IVM by an authorized officer of IVM and constitutes the legal, valid and binding obligation of IVM, enforceable against it in accordance with its terms, as such enforceability may be limited by applicable bankruptcy, insolvency, reorganization, moratorium and similar laws affecting creditors' rights generally.   \n\n    (c) There is no legislation, action, suit, proceeding or investigation pending or, to the best of IVM’s knowledge, threatened, before or by any court, administrative agency, environmental council, arbitrator or governmental authority, body or agency which could reasonably be expected to materially and adversely affect the performance by IVM of its obligations hereunder or which questions the validity, binding effect or enforceability hereof or, any action taken or to be taken by IVM pursuant hereto or any of the transactions contemplated hereby.\n\n    (d) The execution, delivery and performance of this Agreement by VRL has been duly authorized by all necessary corporate action required under relevant law, on the part of the JV Company and do not require any approval or consent of any Person. The execution, delivery and performance by IVM of this Agreement and the consummation of the transactions contemplated hereby, will not result in any violation of any term of its Memorandum of Association or Articles of Association, as the case may be, or any material contract or agreement applicable to it, or of any license, permit, franchise, judgment, writ, injunction or regulation, decree, order, charter, law, ordinance, rule or regulation applicable to it or any of its properties or to any obligations incurred by it or by which it or any of its properties or obligations are bound or affected, or of any determination or award of any arbitrator applicable to it, and will not conflict with, or cause a breach of, or default under, any such term or result in the creation of any lien upon any of its properties or assets. \n\n    (e) The representations, warranties and statements made by IVM in or pursuant to this Agreement are true, complete and correct in all material respects and do not contain any untrue statement of a material fact or omit to state any material fact necessary to make any such representation, warranty or statement, under the circumstances in which it is made, not misleading.  \n\nARTICLE VIII\nSHAREHOLDER MATTERS\n\n8.01\tGeneral Meetings. The Shareholders shall meet on such occasions as may be required by the Organizational Documents or the Companies Act (the “General Meeting”). Each Shareholder hereby agrees to vote (including, if applicable, pursuant to written consent) the Shares owned and controlled by such Shareholder upon all matters submitted to a vote of the General Meeting in conformity with the specific terms and provisions of this Agreement including without limitation the provisions of Section 9.02 below.\n\n8.02\tShareholder Representative; Quorum. Each of VRL and IVM shall be entitled to designate one (1) representative (a “Shareholder Representative”) to represent its interests at General Meetings. RCA shall be entitled to attend General Meetings personally or through a proxy. A Shareholder Representative need not be the same person from meeting to meeting. No business shall be transacted at any General Meeting unless a speci­fied quorum of members is present at the time when the meeting pro­ceeds to transact business. A valid quorum for General Meetings shall be not less than the minimum prescribed by the Companies Act. Provided further that a valid quorum shall be deemed to be constituted only if one Shareholder Representative of VRL and one Shareholder Representative of IVM are present at the beginning and throughout such meeting.  If a valid quorum is not present as required by this Section 8.02, the meeting shall be rescheduled to such time as may be specified by notice of the Board.\n\n8.02\tNotice of Shareholders Meetings. A Shareholders meeting shall be called by the Board at the request of  any Shareholder by giving notice to all of the Shareholders as provided in Section 169 of the Companies Act. The Shareholders shall receive written notice of the date, time and place of Shareholder’s meetings at least twenty-one (21) days prior to the date of such meetings, or such shorter period as the Shareholders shall mutually agree in writing in terms of the Companies Act. Each notice of a General Meeting shall be accompanied by a written agenda for the meeting as well as the text of all resolutions proposed for adoption at such meeting. The Shareholders meeting agenda and proposed resolutions shall be prepared in English by one of the Directors or the Company Secretary, if there is one. Any Shareholder may submit (no less than 7 days prior to the scheduled date of any meeting) agenda items and proposed resolutions for a given meeting and all items so submitted shall be included on the agenda or in the set of proposed resolutions for such meeting, provided, that with the consent in writing of the Shareholder Representatives of IVM and VRL any item of business not included in the agenda may be transacted at the Shareholders meeting.\n\n8.03\tNo Disproportionate Rights. Subject to the Companies Act, each Share shall have one vote and there shall be no disproportionate voting rights. Voting shall always be by way of poll and never by a show of hands.\n\n8.04\tVoting. Except as otherwise required by the Companies Act and subject to the provisions of Section 9.02 below, all decisions of the Shareholders of the JV Company shall be made by simple majority. \n\nARTICLE IX\nBOARD OF DIRECTORS\n\n        9.01 Board of Directors. Subject to the provisions of Section 9.02 below, the business and affairs of the JV Company shall be managed by the Board of Directors, the members of which shall be elected by the Shareholders. The Board shall comprise of four (4) Directors as follows:\n\n    (a) Mr. Ian Ross  \t\t(Nominee of IVM)\n    (b) Mr. Ajay Budhiraja \t(Nominee of IVM)\n    (c) Mr. __________\t(Nominee of VRL)\n    (d) Mr. Ram Chandra Agarwal or his Nominee\n\nNotwithstanding the foregoing, as long as IVM maintains its Shareholding Interest in the JV Company, IVM shall always have a right to nominate two nominees for appointment on the Board of Directors of the JV Company as aforesaid and its committees. As long as VRL maintains its Shareholding Interest in the JV Company, VRL shall always have a right to nominate one nominee for appointment on the Board of Directors of the JV Company. As long as RCA maintains his Shareholding Interest in the JV Company, RCA shall always be entitled to be appointed as a Director on the Board or to nominate one nominee for appointment on the Board of Directors of the JV Company as aforesaid and its committees as aforesaid. The Shareholders shall vote their respective Shares of the JV Company so that the Board of Directors is constituted as aforesaid. None of the Directors shall be Directors whose offices are liable to determination by rotation. In addition, none of the Directors shall be removed and the Shareholders shall not exercise to vote their Shares to remove the Directors, except with the consent of the Shareholder who nominated such Director for appointment. In that event, a Shareholder may cause the removal of his nominee Director/Alternate Director and substitute another person in his/her place, at any time, with or without cause and the other Shareholders agree to vote all of their Shares for such removal only if such removal has been approved by the nominating Shareholder. Similarly, if, at any time, by reason of the death, disability, retirement, removal (with or without cause), resignation or otherwise of a nominee Director a vacancy in the office of the Director has been created, such vacancy shall be filled by the Shareholder who originally nominated the Director for appointment.\n\n        9.02 Day to Day Operations. It is hereby agreed that the IVM nominee Directors on the Board of Directors of the JV Company shall be responsible for the day to day operations of, and all operational and managerial matters relating to the JV Company and shall have a casting or deciding vote with respect to such matters (in the event of a Deadlock), except with respect to (a) matters specified in Exhibit D which shall require affirmative vote as stated in Section 10.03 below, and (b) matters specified in Section 10.02 below. In this regard, Vishal shall provide all support and cooperation to the IVM nominees on the Board to discharge their duties and functions for the day to day operations of, and all operational and managerial matters relating to the JV Company. \n\n        9.03 Chairman. Mr. Ram Chandra Agarwal shall be the non-executive Chairman of the Board of Directors and of the JV Company. The Chairman shall not have a casting or tie-breaking vote whether at Board meetings or Shareholders meetings. In the absence of the Chairman of the Board, one of the Directors present shall be appointed by the Directors in attendance to act as Chairman of the Board. No Director shall be entitled to receive any remuneration from the JV Company other than reasonable expenses incurred in the discharge of his official duties and functions. \n\n        9.04 Committees. The Board may delegate any of its powers other than powers, which by reason of the provisions of the Companies Act cannot be delegated, to committees of the Directors, which shall include the IVM nominee Director and the VRL nominee Director. The Board may, from time to time, revoke and discharge any such committee either wholly or in part and either as to person or persons. Further, no committee of the Directors no matter how constituted or named shall take any decision on any of the business matters described in Section 10.02 of this Agreement. \n\n        9.05 Meetings. Meetings of the Board may be called by any Director as provided in the Articles of Association of the JV Company. Not less than fifteen (15) Business Days’ written notice of every meeting of the Board shall be received by each Director at his usual address in India. In the case of a Director residing outside India, notice of such meeting shall be sent to him at his usual address outside India and also at his address, if any, in India. In the event that any Director (acting reasonably and in good faith) deems that circumstances exist which require a meeting to be convened at shorter notice, such Director may request a meeting of the Board as aforesaid by the giving less than fifteen (15) Business Days prior written notice.\n\n        9.06 Agenda; Quorum. The notice convening a meeting of the Board shall set out the agenda for the meeting listing those items of business to be taken up at the meeting. No item of business shall be transacted at such meeting, unless a quorum of Directors are present. The quorum for Board meetings shall be such number as prescribed by the Companies Act provided that the presence of one (1) nominee Director of IVM and one (1) nominee Director of VRL shall always be required for constituting a quorum for Board meetings. Any item of business not included in the agenda may be transacted at the meeting only with the consent of one (1) nominee Director of IVM and one (1) nominee Director of VRL. \n\n        9.07 Indemnification & Insurance. Subject to the Companies Act, the Parties shall procure the JV Company to indemnify the Directors appointed pursuant to nomination by IVM and Vishal against all losses, liabilities, claims, costs (including attorney fees), expenses, fees, damages, or expenses to the maximum extent permitted by applicable Laws, in respect of the their actions taken for or on behalf of the JV Company. The JV Company shall also procure suitable Director & Officer insurance coverage as required (but in any event such insurance coverage not to be less than Rs. [●] for such Directors.\n\nARTICLE X\nMAJORITY VOTE; DEADLOCK RESOLUTION\n\n10.01\tMajority Vote Requirement. Subject as provided in Sections 10.02, 10.03 and 10.04 below and the Companies Act, the Shareholders shall exercise their respective powers as Shareholders and otherwise in relation to the JV Company to ensure that all matters arising at a meeting of the Board or any committee thereof are decided by a majority of votes of Directors, present and voting. \n\n10.02\tVishal Casting Vote. The Shareholders agree, and the Articles of Association of the JV Company shall so provide, that in the event of a Deadlock Situation with respect to any of the following matters, then to resolve such Deadlock Situation, the Vishal nominee Director (in case of a Deadlock Situation at a meeting of the Board or at any meeting of any committee thereof) or the Shareholder Representative of VRL (in case of a Deadlock Situation at a General Meeting of the JV Company), shall be entitled to a casting, i.e., deciding vote on such matters. \n\n(a)\tMatters relating to the use of Vishal name, brand and logo by the JV Company and/or its customers, except those expressly permitted under this Agreement; and\n\n(b)\tActions to be taken by the JV Company that directly relate to Vishal customers and/or Vishal’s core business. \n\n10.03\tAffirmative Vote Items. The Shareholders agree, and the Articles of Association of the JV Company shall so provide, that no resolution shall be passed or decision taken in respect of the matters listed in Exhibit D annexed to this Agreement whether at a meeting of the Board or at any meeting of any committee thereof, or by the Shareholders at a General Meeting of the JV Company, unless in the case of any such matter to be decided by resolution of the Board or any committee thereof, it has the affirmative votes of the IVM nominee Directors, the VRL nominee Director and RCA, and in the case of any such matter to be decided at a General Meeting of the JV Company, such matter shall require the affirmative vote of the Shareholder Representative of IVM, the Shareholder Representative of VRL, and RCA or his proxy. Any Deadlock Situation with respect to matters listed in Exhibit D shall be referred in the first instance to the Shareholders of the JV Company. If the Shareholder fail to resolve such matters within forty five (45) Business Days of such reference, the Deadlock Situation shall be escalated to the respective Chief Executive Officers (or appropriate officers) of VRL and IVM for resolution. If the Deadlock Situation is still not resolved after sixty (60) Business Days after reference to the respective Chief Executive Officers (or appropriate officers) as aforesaid, then the JV Company shall forthwith be wound up in terms of Section 14.04 below. \n\n10.04\tIVM Casting Vote. The Shareholders agree, and the Articles of Association of the JV Company shall so provide, that in the event of a Deadlock Situation with respect to any of the matters excluding those covered by 10.02 and 10.03 above, then to resolve such Deadlock Situation, the IVM nominee Director (in case of a Deadlock Situation at a meeting of the Board or at any meeting of any committee thereof) or the Shareholder Representative of IVM (in case of a Deadlock Situation at a General Meeting of the JV Company), shall be entitled to a casting, i.e., deciding vote on such matters. \n\n\n10.05\tExercise of Voting Rights. It is hereby agreed that for purposes of voting at General Meetings of the JV Company, VRL and RCA shall vote the VRL Shares and the RCA Shares as a single block of shares, and not separately or individually. It is also agreed that for purposes of voting at Board meetings of the JV Company, the votes of the nominee Director of VRL and RCA shall be treated as a single block voting together, and not separately or individually. IVM and Vishal jointly undertake to ensure that they, their representatives and proxies representing them at the General Meetings of the Shareholders of the JV Company shall at all times exercise their votes and through their respective appointed/nominated Directors (or Alternate Directors) at Board Meetings and otherwise, act in such manner so as to comply with, and to fully and effectually implement the spirit, intent and specific provisions of this Agreement including but not limited with respect to the matters listed out in Sections 10.02, 10.03 and 10.04 above. No resolution shall be passed by the Board or a committee of the Board of Directors or at General Meetings, as the case may be, in contravention of Sections 10.02, 10.03 and 10.04.\n\nARTICLE XI\nTRANSFERS\n\n11.01\tGeneral Restrictions on Transfers. Subject to Section 5.05 and further subject to any permitted transaction(s) by this Agreement, the Shareholders agree that for a period of thirty six (36) calendar months from the Closing Date (“Lock-in-Period”), no Shareholder shall effect a Transfer in  any manner whatsoever. Notwithstanding the foregoing, Vishal may exit their shareholding of the JV Company at any time after the second anniversary of the Closing Date, if the JV Company fails to commence business or fails to achieve [40%] of its projected revenues as per milestones stated in the current Business Plan. The Shareholders further agree that after the expiry of the Lock-in-Period and during the term of this Agreement, none of the Shareholders shall effect a Transfer, in any manner whatsoever, except in accordance with the terms of this Agreement. Compliance with the provisions of this Agreement shall be a condition precedent to the registration by the JV Company of any Transfer in its Register of Members. \n\n11.02\tMutual Right of First Refusal \n\n(a)\tIf at any time after the expiry of thirty six (36) calendar months from the Closing Date any Shareholder proposes to sell or otherwise effect a Transfer of its/his Shares in a manner permitted by this Agreement (hereafter the “Selling Shareholder”), it/he shall do so subject to a mutual right of first refusal hereunder. Such Selling Shareholder shall give notice in writing to non-Selling Shareholders indicating the number of Shares offered, the price at which such Shares are offered and such other particulars as it/she may wish to specify in the notice (hereafter the “Selling Shareholder Notice”). \n\nWithin a period of 45 Business Days of receipt of the Selling Shareholder Notice, a non-Selling Shareholder may either accept the offer and exercise his/its right with respect to his/its pro rata portion of the Shares so offered by the Selling Shareholder, subject to his/its mutual right of co-sale hereunder or indicate his/its non-acceptance. If a non-Selling Shareholder gives the Selling Shareholder notice that he/it desires to purchase his/its pro rata portion of the Shares so offered by the Selling Shareholder, then the price for such Shares shall be the fair market value for such Shares as determined by an independent firm of chartered accountants (“Independent Valuer”) mutually agreed upon by the Selling Shareholder and the non-Selling Shareholder (failing such agreement, the Independent Valuer shall be appointed by [●]). \n\nThe Independent Valuer shall be instructed to determine the fair market value of the Shares by valuing the JV Company (including any subsidiary of the JV Company) as a whole on a going concern basis as at the end of the month before the month in which the Independent Valuer is appointed. The fair market value of each Share will be the proportionate amount of the value of the JV Company. The Independent Valuer's determination will be final and binding on the Parties. The Independent Valuer's cost and expenses will be borne by the JV Company.\n\nThe payment for the Selling Shareholder’s such Shares shall be by cheque or wire transfer, against delivery of the Selling Shareholder’s offered Shares, to be purchased at a place agreed upon between the Parties and at the time of the scheduled closing therefor no later than sixty (60) Business Days after determination of the fair market value. \n\n(b)\tIf  a non-Selling Shareholder does not respond within the period of 45 Business Days of receipt of the Selling Shareholder Notice, he/it shall be deemed to have waived his/its right to purchase the Shares, and the Selling Shareholder shall be free to sell the Shares to any third party if he/it so desires (provided that such third party has the financial resources sufficient to bear, and also assumes all obligations of the Selling Shareholder under this Agreement by executing a Deed of Adherence) within a period of sixty (60) Business Days thereafter.\n\n11.03\tRight of Co-Sale. A non-Selling Shareholder may elect not to exercise its right of first refusal pursuant to this Article XI and may elect to exercise its right of co-sale by notifying the Selling Shareholder within 45 Business Days of receipt of the Selling Shareholder Notice and such non-Selling Shareholder shall have the right to participate in such sale of Shares of the Selling Shareholder on the same terms and conditions. The non-Selling Shareholder may include in the Selling Shareholder’s proposed sale up to that number of Shares his/its Shareholding Interest bears to the numbers of Shares proposed to be sold by the Selling Shareholder. To the extent that any prospective purchaser otherwise refuses to purchase Shares from the non-Selling Shareholder exercising his/its co-sale rights hereunder, the Selling Shareholder shall not sell to such prospective purchaser any Shares unless and until, simultaneously with such sale, the prospective purchaser shall purchase that number of the non-Selling Shareholder’s Shares calculated pursuant to this sub-Section on the same terms specified in the Selling Shareholder Notice. \n\n11.04\tSubsequent Sales. A Shareholder’s exercise or non-exercise of his/its right of first refusal hereunder to participate in one or more sales of shares made by a Selling Shareholder shall not affect such Shareholder’s rights to participate in subsequent sales of shares pursuant to this Article XI.\n\n\nARTICLE XII\nDIVIDEND POLICY AND FINANCIAL INFORMATION\n\n12.01\tDividends: All dividends for each financial year shall be distributed to the Shareholders in accordance with each Shareholder's Shareholder Interest within a reasonable period of time after the declaration of such dividends.\n\n12.02.\tThe JV Company shall furnish to the Shareholders the following documents:\n\nAudited Financial Statements\n\nAs soon as practicable after the end of each financial year of the JV Company, and in any event within ninety (90) days thereafter, a consolidated balance sheet/statement of income of the JV Company, as at the end of such financial year, prepared in accordance with India GAAP, all in reasonable detail. Such financial statements shall be accompanied by a report and opinion thereon by the independent statutory auditor appointed by the Board and approved by the Shareholders of the JV Company.\n\nUnaudited Financial Statements\n\nWithin thirty (30) days following the end of each financial quarter, an unaudited consolidated balance sheet of the JV Company as of such financial quarter, covering such financial quarter, prepared in accordance with India GAAP.\n\nMonthly Reports\n\nAs soon as practicable after the end of each month during the financial year of the JV Company, and in any event within fifteen (15) days following the end of each month, a management report in form and substance acceptable to the Shareholders.\n\nBusiness Plan \n\nThe Board of Directors of the JV Company shall endeavour to approve the Business Plan (or any amendments thereto) as prepared and submitted by IVM in consultation with Vishal within thirty (30) Business Days of submission of the Business Plan provided that the Board may (a) approve the Business Plan subject to conditions to be satisfied/fulfilled by the JV Company/Parties, or (b) request IVM for additional information or analysis as would afford the Board an adequate evaluation and consideration of the Business Plan, in which event IVM shall endevour to promptly comply with such request. \n\nAdditional Information\n\nIn case a Shareholder requests for additional information regarding the business of the JV Company then the Shareholders shall procure the JV Company to comply with such requests for additional information within a reasonable period of receipt of the request.\n\n12.03\tRight of inspection.  So long as IVM holds Shares in the share capital of the JV Company, IVM shall have the right to inspect the records and books of accounts of the JV Company through accountants of its choice at reasonable times and after providing reasonable notice. IVM may direct the JV Company to engage an independent accountant selected by IVM to conduct a special audit of the affairs, finances and accounts of the JV Company, at the expense of IVM. \n\nARTICLE XIII\nCONFIDENTIALITY\n\n13.01\tThe Parties recognize that each of them will be given and have access to confidential and proprietary information of the other Parties. Each Party undertakes not to use any confidential information of the other Parties for their own corporate purposes or any other purpose without the prior written consent of the Party owning such information and shall use its/his best efforts to keep confidential and not to disclose to any third party any such confidential and proprietary information. The Parties shall take all such steps as are necessary to ensure that their respective Directors, employees, Relatives, officers and any other persons to whom the above mentioned information is disclosed are bound by these covenants. The obligations of confidentiality shall not apply to any information that:\n\n(i)\twas developed independently by a Party without utilizing the confidential information of the other Parties;\n\n(ii)\twas known to a Party prior to its disclosure by the disclosing Party;\n\n(iii)\thas become generally available to the public (other than due to the disclosure by the receiving Party);\n\n(iv)\tmay be required in any report, statement or testimony submitted to any governmental regulatory body;\n\n(v)\tmay be required in response to any summons or in connection with any judicial proceedings; or\n\n(vi)\tmay be required to comply with any law, order, regulation or ruling applicable to any Party hereto;\n\n\tProvided that prior to any disclosure in respect of a request to disclose confidential information under subsections (iv), (v) and (vi), a Party must first notify the Party owning such confidential information.\n\n13.02\tThe obligations of the Parties under this Article shall remain in effect throughout the term of this Agreement and so long as the JV Company exists and for a period of [5 years thereafter]. These obligations shall not be affected by any Transfer of Shares.  \n\nARTICLE XIV\nTERM AND TERMINATION\n\n14.01\tTerm. This Agreement shall remain in full force and effect for so long as any of the Shareholders continues to own Shares of the JV Company or as otherwise terminated by mutual written agreement of the Shareholders or otherwise pursuant to the terms of this Agreement.\n\n14.02\tEvents of Termination. Subject to Sections 4.01, in the event of: \n\n(a)\tany Shareholder committing any material breach of the provisions of this Agreement (“Defaulting Shareholder”), which breach is not cured within sixty (60) days of receipt of notice by a non Defaulting Shareholder requesting the Defaulting Shareholder, to cure such breach (in which case all rights attaching to Shares held by the Defaulting Shareholder will be suspended until the breach is remedied or cured); or \n\n(b)\tinitiation of winding up/liquidation/bankruptcy proceedings against a Shareholder (“Defaulting Shareholder”), which proceedings are not set aside by an uncontroverted order of a court of competent jurisdiction within one hundred twenty (120) Business Days from the date of such initiation,\n\nthen notwithstanding and in addition to such other remedies as may be provided under this Agreement or under applicable laws, (including without limitation the indemnity obligations under Section 15.10) then the non Defaulting Shareholder shall be entitled to terminate this Agreement. In that event, the non Defaulting Shareholder shall have an option but not the obligation to either: \n\n(i) require the JV Company to buy back all (and not less than all) of the Shares (including outstanding options and redemptions) of the JV Company then owned by the non Defaulting Shareholder by given written notice (the “Buyback Notice”) to the JV Company, or \n\n(ii) require the Defaulting Shareholder to purchase all (and not less than all) of the Shares (including outstanding options and redemptions) of the JV Company then owned by the non Defaulting Shareholder by giving written notice (the “Put Notice”) to the Defaulting Shareholder; or \n\n(iii) require the Defaulting Shareholder to sell to the non Defaulting Shareholder all (and not less than all) of the Shares (including outstanding options and redemptions) of the JV Company then owned by the Defaulting Shareholder by giving a Call Notice written notice (the “Call Notice I”) to the Defaulting Shareholder. \n \nUpon the issue of either a Buyback Notice or a Put Notice, the purchase price for such Shares shall be [one hundred twenty percent (120%)] of the fair market value of the Shares held by the non Defaulting Party and such fair market value of the Shares shall be determined by an Independent Valuer appointed in accordance with the provisions of Section 11.02 above. Upon the issue of a Call Notice, the purchase price for such Shares shall be such fair market value of the Shares as determined by an Independent Valuer appointed in accordance with the provisions of Section 11.02 above. \n\nProvided that where VRL Shares and RCA Shares are sold pursuant to the provisions of this Section as aforesaid, IVM shall procure that within ninety (90) Business Days of such sale, the JV Company ceases to use any name, or brand or logo of Vishal. Provided, further, that VRL and RCA shall enter into and execute appropriate agreements as may be required by the JV Company to continue to meet its contractual obligations to its existing customers/clients.\n\n14.04\tWinding Up. Without prejudice to the provisions of Sections 14.01 and 14.02 above, this Agreement shall terminate upon  a resolution being passed by the Shareholders for the winding up of the JV Company. In such event, the Parties shall endeavour to agree on a suitable basis for dealing with the interests and assets of the JV Company but subject thereto:\n\n    (a) the Chief Operating Officer of the JV Company or any other authorized officer of the JV Company shall develop and submit a plan to the Board for winding down the business operations of the JV Company;\n\n    (b) the Parties shall co-operate (but without any obligation to provide any additional finance) with the JV Company for the purpose of enabling all existing obligations of the JV Company to be completed insofar as reasonable and the JV Company’s resources allow. IVM and Vishal shall consult together with a view to outstanding contracts of the JV Company within the business being novated or re-allocated in a suitable manner subject to a valuation of such contracts. Such contracts shall subject to mutual agreement of the Parties be novated or re-allocated to IVM and/or its Affiliates at the fair market price;\n\n    (c) no new contractual obligation for the supply of products or services shall be assumed by  the JV Company;\n\n    (d) the Parties shall procure that the JV Company shall as soon as practicable be wound up and the JV Company shall be wound-up in accordance with the provisions of the Companies Act;\n\n    (e) IVM and Vishal shall be free to compete in any way with the business hitherto carried on by the JV Company; \n\n    (f) Any non cash assets of the JV Company shall be valued at fair market value and, to the extent necessary, determined by an independent appraiser, and shall be distributed among the Shareholders in their respective Shareholding Interest. Any intangible assets owned by the JV Company and any customer/client data base developed and/or created by the JV Company (not otherwise licensed by VRL to the JV Company) shall be considered to be jointly owned by the Parties (it being understood and agreed that any corporate name, trademark or tradename of a Party shall in no way constitute the property of the JV Company), and, after the dissolution of the JV Company, each Party shall have the right to use, sell, license or transfer any such assets (subject to the other Parties’ right thereto) without payment to the other Parties of any royalties or considerations therefor, subject to the terms and provisions of this Agreement and agreements contemplated hereby or in connection herewith; and\n\n    (g) if there is any surplus, after payment of all debts and liabilities of the JV Company, the Parties shall cause the liquidator to distribute such surplus in accordance with the then respective Shareholding Interest of the Parties.\n\n14.05\tTermination of this Agreement for any reason whatsoever shall not release the Parties from any liability or obligation in respect of any matters, undertakings or conditions which shall not have been done, observed or performed by any one of them prior to such termination or which, at the said time has already accrued to the concerned Party. The Parties agree that provisions contained in this Agreement which are required to give effect to Articles, Sections or Sub-Sections which shall survive termination shall also survive termination of this Agreement. \n\n   ARTICLE XV\nMISCELLANEOUS\n\n15.01\tEquitable Relief. The Parties hereto agree and declare that legal remedies may be inadequate to enforce the provisions of this Agreement and that equitable relief, including specific performance and injunctive relief, may be used to enforce the provisions of this Agreement.\n\n15.02\tDispute Resolution. The Parties agree that instead of seeking relief from a court, they will attempt in good faith to resolve any dispute or controversy that arises out of this Agreement, or the performance, breach, validity, interpretation or enforcement thereof (any such dispute or controversy, a “Dispute”) first among themselves through informal discussions and negotiations and, if unsuccessful, through binding arbitration, in accordance with the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 of India, by a sole arbitrator appointed by mutual written agreement of the Parties within sixty (60) days of the Dispute, or such other extended period as the Parties agree in writing, failing which the sole arbitrator shall be appointed by the High Court of Delhi on application of any Party. During the pendency of any Dispute resolution by management or any arbitration, the Parties shall continue to perform their obligations not under Dispute under this Agreement.\n\n15.03\tNotices. All notices that are required or may be given pursuant to this Agreement must be in writing and delivered personally, by a recognized national courier/delivery service, by facsimile or by registered AD or certified mail, postage prepaid, to the Parties at the Parties’ respective addresses stated above in this Agreement (or to the attention of such other person or such other address as any party may provide to the other Parties by notice in accordance with this Section 15.03. \n\n15.04\tCounterparts. This Agreement may be executed in counterparts, each of which when so executed and delivered shall be deemed an original and all of which together shall constitute one and the same instrument.\n\n\t15.05\tGoverning Law. This Agreement shall be governed by the laws of the Republic of India.\n15.06  Waiver and Severability.  No failure or delay by a Party in exercising any right or power of remedy under this Agreement shall operate as a waiver thereof, nor shall any single or partial exercise of any other right or power or remedy preclude any other further exercise therof or the exercise of any other right or power or remedy. In the event any one or more of the provisions of this Agreement shall for any reason be held to be invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions of this Agreement shall be unimpaired, and the invalid or unenforceable provision shall be replaced by a mutually acceptable provision that, being valid and enforceable, comes closest to the intention of the Parties underlying the invalid or unenforceable provision.\n\n15.07\tHeadings. The Article, Sections and Sub-Section headings contained in this Agreement are for reference purposes only and shall not affect in any way the meaning or interpretation of this Agreement.\n\n\t15.08\tAfter-Acquired Shares. All of the provisions of this Agreement shall apply to all Shares now owned or hereafter issued or transferred to a Shareholder in consequence of any additional issuance, purchase, exchange, reclassification or Transfer of shares, corporate reorganization, or any other recapitalization, or consolidation, or share split, or which are acquired by a Shareholder in any other manner.\n\n15.09\tConflict of Terms.  If there shall be an inconsistency or conflict in the terms of this Agreement and the provisions of the Memorandum of Association and/or Articles of Association of the JV Company, the Parties shall endeavor to amend the Memorandum of Association or Articles of Association, as the case may be, so as to reflect the terms of this Agreement, so far as permitted by applicable law. \n\n15.10\tIndemnity.  All representations, warranties, covenants, undertakings made by a Party in this Agreement shall be deemed to have been relied on by the other Parties, notwithstanding any investigation made by such other Parties.  Each Shareholder hereby indemnifies, defends and holds harmless the other Shareholders and their respective successors, administrators, executors, assigns and Affiliates (and their respective successors and assigns), from and against any and all damages, liabilities, obligations, losses, claims cost charges or other expenses of every kind and character, whether absolute, accrued, or contingent, including but not limited to attorneys’ fees and litigation costs, incurred or which may be sustained by any of them in any capacity and resulting from or relating to the breach by such Shareholder of its representations, warranties, covenants and undertakings contained herein. \n\n15.11\tDisclosures. No Party shall make any public statement or disclose the existence of this Agreement or its terms to any third party without the consent of the other Parties except for any statutory disclosures that might need to be made by any Party as per law\n\n15.12\tEntire Agreement and Amendment. This Agreement and all the Exhibits hereto constitute the entire agreement between the Parties with respect to the matters dealt with herein and supersedes any previous agreement between the Parties in relation to such matters. No modification or amendment to this Agreement and no waiver of any of the terms or conditions hereof shall be valid or binding unless made in writing and duly executed by all the Parties hereto.\n[SIGNATURE PAGES FOLLOW]\nIN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Parties hereto have caused this Agreement to be executed and delivered on its behalf by its authorized officer as of the date first above written.\n\n\nWitnesses\t\t\t\t\tFor and behalf of: \n\t[Name of Hollard Entity], Netherlands \n\nName: ______________________\t\tSignature: _______________________\nAddress: ___________________\t\tName: __________________________\n\tDesignation: ______________________\n\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFor and on behalf of: \nVISHAL RETAIL LIMITED\nName: ___________________\t\t\t\nAddress:_____________\t\t\tSignature:_______________________\n\tName: \n\tDesignation:\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRAM CHANDRA AGARWAL\t\n\nName:________________\t\t\tSignature:_______________________\nAddress:_____________\tName: RAM CHANDRA AGARWAL\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\nEXHIBIT A\nDEED OF ADHERENCE\n\nTHIS DEED OF ADHERENCE (\"Deed\") is made on the ___ day of ____, by and among: \n\n[                    ] of [                    ] (hereinafter referred to as the “Covenantor”), which expression shall where the context so admits include its successors and permitted assigns, of the FIRST PART;\n\nAND\n[Name of Hollard Insurance Entity], a trust established under the laws of the Netherlands, having its principal office at ________________________, Netherlands (hereinafter referred to as “IVM”, which expression shall where the context so admits include its successors, administrators, trustees and assigns), of the SECOND PART;\n\nAND\n\nVISHAL RETAIL LIMITED, a company incorporated under the Companies Act, 1956, having its registered office at ________________________, India, through its authorized signatory, Mr. ______________  (hereinafter referred to as “VRL” which expression shall where the context so admits include its successors and permitted assigns), of the THIRD PART;\n\nAND\n\nMR. RAM CHANDRA AGARWAL, son of Late Shri Kishan Gopal Agarwal, resident of B1-801, Lagoon Apartments, Ambience Islands, Gurgaon, Haryana, India (hereinafter referred to as “RCA” which expression shall where the context so admits include his heirs, legal representatives and permitted assigns), of the FOURTH PART.\n\nThis Deed is executed pursuant to the Share Subscription and Shareholders Agreement dated _______, 2008 executed among [names of parties] (hereafter the “Agreement”) \n\nWITNESSETH as follows:-\n\n    1. Capitalised terms used in this Deed and not otherwise defined herein shall have the same meaning as set out in the Agreement.\n    2. [_________ the \"Transferor\"] proposes to transfer [  ] Shares held by it in the JV Company to the Covenantor pursuant to Article X of the Agreement, the provisions of which require a Transferee to assume all obligations of the transferring Shareholders by executing this Deed as a condition precedent to the Transfer of Shares.\n    3. The Covenantor hereby confirms that it has been provided a copy of the Agreement and hereby covenants with each of the Parties to the Agreement to assume the obligations of the Transferor under the Agreement and to observe, perform and be bound by all the terms of the Agreement applicable to the Transferor to the intent and effect that the Covenantor shall be deemed to be a Party to the Agreement as if it were such Transferor for the purposes of the Agreement.\n    4. This Deed shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India.\n\nEXECUTED as a deed the day and year first before written.\n\n\nBy: \n\n\n[Name of the Parties and Witnesses]\nExhibit B\nACCESSION AGREEMENT\n\nTo:      \n\n1.\t[IVM]\n[Address]\n\n2.\tVISHAL RETAIL LIMITED\n\t[Address]\n\n3.\tMR. RAM CHANDRA AGARWAL\nB1-801, Lagoon Apartments, \nAmbience Islands, \nGurgaon, Haryana, \nIndia \n\nFrom:\t\n\n[Name of JV Company]\n[Address]\n\n[Date]\n\nRE:\tJOINT VENTURE AND SHAREHOLDERS AGREEMENT DATED [●] AMONG [IVM], VISHAL RETAIL LIMITED AND MR. RAM CHANDRA AGARWAL (THE “AGREEMENT”) \n\nTerms used herein which are defined in the Agreement shall have the same meaning herein as in the Agreement.\n\nWe refer to Section 4.01(h)(ii) of the Agreement.\n\nWe, [Name of JV Company], (Registered no. [ ]), having our registered office at [Registered Office] hereby confirm that we have been provided a copy of the Agreement and hereby covenant with each of the Parties to the Agreement to observe, perform and be bound by all the terms of the Agreement applicable to the “JV Company” in accordance with Section 4.01(h)(ii) of the Agreement as if we were originally a Party thereto, to the intent and effect that we shall be deemed to be a Party to the Agreement.\n\nOur address for notices for the purposes of Section 15.03 is:\n\n[Insert Address]\n\n\n\nThis document shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India.\n\n\nFor and on behalf of [Name of JV Company]\n\nBy:\t\t\t\t\t\t[Vide Resolution of the Board of Directors\nDesignation: \t\t\t\t\tdated ___________]\n\n\nWitnesses:\n\nSignature:_______________________\nName: _________________________\t\t\t\nAddress:________________________\t\t\t\n\n\nSignature:_______________________\nName: _________________________\t\t\t\nAddress:________________________\t\t\t\n\nExhibit C\n[On the letterhead of the concerned entity]\nTO WHOMSOEVER IT MAY CONCERN\nSub.:  No-Objection Certificate\n\n\tWe, hereby unconditionally and irrevocably consent to [Name of Hollard Insurance Entity] and/or its holding companies, subsidiaries, affiliates or sister concerns (each a “IVM Entity”) making, from time to time, directly or indirectly, any investments in or entering into any joint venture, collaboration or other agreements or arrangements with any persons or companies in India (including setting up a subsidiary) carrying on any business or activities in India in any manner whatsoever, including without limitation in the same, similar or allied business or activities  as the business / activities being carried out / to be carried out by [Insert Name of JV Company] or any of its affiliates, from time to time. \n\nThis No-Objection Certificate shall be deemed to be a declaration of no-objection which may be required to be filed by any IVM Entity before the Foreign Investment Promotion Board, the Reserve Bank of India or any other central or state government or regulatory authority, department or entity in India, in connection with obtaining approval for its investment or setting up of a wholly owned subsidiary, joint venture or tie-up in India through investment in shares, debentures or any other securities or instruments, or a technical collaboration or a trademark agreement or investment by whatever name called, or any other proposal to carry on any business in any manner whatsoever, in conjunction with another Indian company, entity or individual in India or by itself or through its own subsidiaries or affiliates or associate companies. \n\nThis No-Objection Certificate shall also deemed to be issued pursuant to the requirements laid down by Press Note 1 (2005 Series), read with Press Note 18 (1998 Series), issued by the Ministry of Commerce and  Industry, Government of India, (as amended from time to time) and any other guidelines, press releases and other official documents issued by the Foreign Investment Promotion Board, the Reserve Bank of India, and/or any other central or state government or regulatory authority, department or entity in India.\n\nYours faithfully,\nFor and on behalf of [insert name of entity]\n\n\n____________________\nName:\nDesignation:\n \nExhibit D\n\nAffirmative Vote Matters \n\n        (a) Any proposal for amendment or change of the rights, preferences, privileges or powers of, or the restrictions provided for the benefit of, the IVM Shares, VRL Shares and RCA Shares (and any action for reclassifying issued shares into shares having preferences or priority as to dividends or assets senior to or on a parity with the IVM Shares, VRL Shares and RCA Shares);\n\n        (b) Any proposal for authorizing, creating or issuing shares of any class having preferences superior to or on a parity with the IVM Shares, VRL Shares and RCA Shares; \n\n        (c) Any proposal for amendment of the Memorandum of Association of the JV Company and/or Articles of Association of the JV Company; \n\n        (d) Any proposal for the sale of all or substantially all of the JV Company’s assets or those of any of its subsidiaries; \n\n        (e) Any proposal for liquidation or dissolution of the JV Company;\n\n        (f) Any proposal or recommendation for declaration or payment of a dividend; \n\n        (g) Any proposal for Transfer of Shares which does not comply with the provisions of this Agreement; \n\n        (h) Any proposal for adoption of any equity incentive plan or any Employee Stock Option Scheme; \n\n        (i) Any proposal for change in the JV Company’s financial or tax accounting policies; \n\n        (j) Any change in the authorized capital; \n\n        (k) Entering into any transactions with any Shareholder including their Affiliates, Director(s) or relatives of the Shareholders/Promoters or Director(s) or other related companies, entities or firms in which the Shareholders or Director(s) of the JV Company directly or indirectly have an interest or any other transaction which is not at arms length;\n\n        (l) Any proposal for changing the business of the JV Company or the entering into of any new business; \n\n        (m) Any issue of New Shares; \n\n        (n) Any proposal for increasing or decreasing the number of Directors or appointment of directors other than as envisaged in this Agreement; \n\n        (o) Appointment, dismissal or change in the remuneration of the General Manager and Finance Manager of the JV Company; \n\n        (p) Any proposal for significant corporate transactions, including the incurrence of capital expenditure or indebtedness, in excess of the limits specified in the then current Business Plan;\n\n        (q) Approval of the annual accounts;  \n\n        (r) Any resolution for reducing the share capital of the JV Company and/or for buy back of the Shares of the JV Company; \n\n        (s) approval or amendment of the Budget;\n\n        (t) Any proposal for a merger, amalgamation, reorganization, restructuring or consolidation of the JV Company (regardless of whether the JV Company is the entity surviving such merger, amalgamation, reorganization, restructuring or consolidation);\n\n        (u) Issue of any press releases with respect to the joint venture among the Parties or the JV Company;\n\n        (v) approval or amendment of the Business Plan; and\n\n        (w) Any proposal to appoint/remove/change the auditors of the JV Company."});
